regexec.c: the regset search sets up each regex only when it tries it

onig_regset_search in ONIG_REGSET_POSITION_LEAD mode used to set up every
regex of the set before it searched: adjust the match parameters, resize
the region, and MATCH_ARG_INIT the match arguments, then free them all at
the end. Most searches stop after trying a few of the regexes, so most of
that work was thrown away. With this patch, a search in that mode, with
start < end, sets up a regex the first time the search tries a match with
it (regset_lazy_setup), and frees and clears only the regexes it set up.
The set keeps a generation number per regex (tm_igen) and the list of the
regexes set up in the current search (tm_used); each search starts a new
generation, so nothing carries over from one search to the next. The
empty string and ONIG_REGSET_REGEX_LEAD keep the eager setup. The regions
of regexes a search didn't try keep their earlier contents.

See rust/vendor/README.md.

